WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
So as I grew up there, yes, I did form a
community, but I think for me, there

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.020
was always something within that made me
feel out of place.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:13.300
Like, hi, everyone. My name is Michelle

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:19.480
Barure. I was basically born in Zimbabwe
and I grew up in

5
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.280
South Africa. One of my favorite quotes by
Nelson Mandela says, let your decisions

6
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.400
reflect your hopes and not your fears.

7
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.500
And that is exactly how I mustered up the
carriage to travel from South Africa

8
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.700
to Zimbabwe to Ethiopia, and finally to
Kigali, Rwanda, to study at

9
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.880
the African Leadership University.

10
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.680
Because of how I grew

11
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.000
up, I basically grew up a bit in Zimbabwe
and then the rest of my life afterwards,

12
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.700
my entire high school and a bit of my
primary school was done in South Africa.

13
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.900
So as I grew up there, yes, I did form a
community, but I think for me, there

14
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.100
was always something within that made me
feel out of place.

15
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.700
Like, this isn't my home. It's a temporary
place that I'm staying in.

16
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.000
And I'd always think, like, why can't I go
back to Zimbabwe and stay there?

17
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.560
Because that's my home. That's where I'd
feel most comfortable.

18
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.600
That's not how I felt in South Africa.

19
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.980
So I think that probably sparked something
in me that, OK, why can't we stay

20
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.160
in Zimbabwe? And now you look at Zimbabwe,
you can see there's a bad economic

21
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.320
state, bad governance. Everything is just
terrible in terms of supply to water.

22
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.220
People can't even get water running
through their taps.

23
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.200
And it's just a lot that just goes on.

24
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.600
And I think that's something that is
influencing the mission that I will probably

25
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.780
have. I'm looking towards how we can make
Zimbabwe a better place so that all

26
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.280
the governments can actually come back
home and not have to leave the country.

27
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.760
In 2023, we discovered that my younger
sister, Masha Stansles, was swelling

28
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.460
up and blocking her airway.

29
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.640
In that moment, I realized we had two
options.

30
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:08.500
We could either go to a public hospital,
but that would mean waiting in a long

31
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.220
queue and having no guarantee of actually
seeing a doctor and receiving a solution

32
00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:17.740
in the same day. Our second option would
be to go to a private hospital that

33
00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:22.620
can be accessed through a health insurance
or paying cash at that moment.

34
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.500
And that would mean that you would pay an
excessively large amount just to

35
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.720
receive a consultation and then pay
another excessively large amount to get

36
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.000
the solution. Then I thought to myself, as
an African individual who may not

37
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.760
know about health insurance or cannot
access a private hospital, what would

38
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.100
happen in such a dire situation?

39
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.260
And that is where my mission comes in.

40
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.940
My mission is to increase the quality of
health care systems in Zimbabwean

41
00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.320
communities, as well as to increase the
accessibility to health care for all

42
00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.820
individuals living in Zimbabwean
communities.

43
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.940
I hope to develop a model that can be applied
all over Africa and other communities

44
00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.980
that are facing the same situation.

45
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.980
I know that in order to see the Zimbabwe
that I desire to see that is transformed,

46
00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.960
I cannot do that by myself.

47
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.420
But I am looking forward towards
collaborating with other individuals that

48
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:24.240
have different missions that will aim
towards transforming Zimbabwe and Africa

49
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.100
as a whole.
